m(4,"Subtitle","What is the article's subtitle?","Citizens can avoid polarization and make sound decisions",["Why elites must save democracy from its citizens","Populism and the end of deliberative politics","The people against the experts in a post-truth age"],"Subtitle: “Citizens can avoid polarization and make sound decisions.”");
m(4,"Overload","Counterintuitively, what problem do the authors say faces democracy?","There are more opportunities than ever for citizens to express their views",["Citizens have fewer and fewer ways to express their views","Elections are held too rarely","Citizens have lost all interest in politics"],"“The sheer quantitative overabundance overloads policy-makers and citizens.”");
