lv(2,vf,4,"As elites get more uncivil, citizens pay more attention to the content of arguments.",false,"They follow partisan cues or drop out.");
lv(3,ty,4,"Term for government by the wise, which skeptical readings of citizen competence can support",["epistocracy"],"Opposed to democracy.");
// ---- S15 · 5. What deliberation research finds
lv(3,m,5,"Case","A group of like-minded partisans discusses an issue in a well-run deliberative setting. What do the authors say will tend to happen?","They become less extreme",["They become more extreme","Nothing changes","They stop talking to each other"],"Without deliberative conditions like-minded groups become more extreme; with them extremism is ameliorated, even more when different sides are engaged.");
lv(3,m,5,"Case","In the “What's Next California” deliberative poll, support for a part-time legislature with part-time pay dropped massively. What does this show?","Deliberation makes judgments more considered and counteracts populist proposals",["Citizens dislike legislators","Deliberation always reduces support for reforms","Polls have no effect"],"Deliberation makes judgments more considered and more consistent with people's values.");
lv(3,m,5,"Case","A government wants a high-quality deliberation with ordinary people. Which design features do the authors favour?","Balanced information, expert testimony and a facilitator",["Open social-media voting","A single expert speech","A debate among party leaders only"],"They help ordinary people deliberate well.");
